# Coding conventions

This repo is a Sage 11 WordPress theme (Blade, PHP 8.3, Tailwind v4, Vite), not a Next.js or Supabase app. Do not add App Router, RSC, Genql, next-safe-action, or Shadcn unless Matt asks for a separate project.

Matt is a marketer who prefers working directly in code. Keep diffs small, copy in wp-admin fields, and avoid inventing admin UIs.

## Key principles

- Write concise, accurate code. Prefer functional, declarative style. Avoid classes unless WordPress or Acorn requires one.
- Prefer iteration and small helpers over duplication.
- Use descriptive names with auxiliary verbs: `isLoading`, `hasError`, `doesValidate`, `shouldRedirect`.
- Directories and view/partial filenames: lowercase with dashes (`partials/work-card.blade.php`).
- PHP: named functions in the `App` namespace. JS: named exports for modules (`export function initWorkTools`).
- Receive an object, return an object (RORO) for helpers with several parameters.

## PHP and JavaScript

- Use `function` for pure helpers. Omit semicolons in JS.
- Prefer PHP 8 typed functions and `interface` only when a real contract is needed; do not add TypeScript to this theme.
- File order: public API / exported functions, helpers, static content, types (JSDoc).
- Single-line conditionals omit braces: `if ($hasError) return $errors;`
- Match existing Pint style in `app/`. Run `vendor/bin/pint` after PHP edits.

## Error handling and validation

- Guard clauses first; happy path last. Avoid nested `else`.
- Return user-facing errors as values (arrays, redirects with transients) for expected contact/form failures. Do not throw for normal validation misses.
- Log unexpected failures; show a short, human message (no stack traces on the public site).
- Sanitize and unslash all request input (`sanitize_text_field`, `sanitize_email`, nonces) before use.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, or `.deploy-keys/`. Tokens live in wp-admin or environment variables (`MH_GITHUB_TOKEN`).

## Blade, templates, and WordPress

- Follow the WordPress template hierarchy. Chrome lives in `resources/views/sections/`; reusable chunks in `partials/`; named pages in `template-*.blade.php`.
- Visitor-facing sentences belong in **Page content (theme)** via `app/page-fields.php` and `\App\field()`, not hardcoded in Blade.
- Do not add Kadence, page builders, a theme-options screen, or extra `app/*.php` modules unless Matt asks. Portfolio logic stays in `app/portfolio.php`, `app/contact.php`, `app/Github.php`, `app/page-fields.php`.
- After Blade edits in Cloud, run `cd ~/wp-site && wp acorn view:clear`.
- Prefer server-rendered HTML. Keep `resources/js/` small and for Web APIs (dark mode, copy, search filters). Do not fetch page content in JS when PHP/Blade can render it.

## Front-end (Tailwind, a11y)

- Style with Tailwind v4 utilities in Blade. Shared theme look lives in `resources/css/portfolio.css`; do not introduce a CSS-in-JS layer.
- Mobile-first responsive classes. Preserve existing Inter / IBM Plex and navy/blue/gray palette.
- Dark mode is `html.mh-dark` plus the header toggle; respect `prefers-color-scheme` until the visitor saves a choice.
- Images: explicit width/height or aspect ratio, lazy-load below the fold, WebP when adding new assets.
- Keyboard access, visible focus, and ARIA only when native HTML is not enough (`aria-label`, `aria-pressed` on icon-only buttons). Meet WCAG contrast on new UI.
- Static copy and option lists sit in PHP field defaults or a content array at the bottom of the file, not inline in the middle of markup loops.

## JS modules

- `function`, not `const fn = () =>`, for named module functions.
- Minimize new global state. Prefer `querySelector` + listeners inside `init*` functions imported from `resources/js/app.js`.
- Handle missing DOM early: `if (!root) return;`
- Do not add React, Radix, or Shadcn to this theme.

## Data and APIs

- WordPress APIs, transients, and WP-CLI — not Supabase or GraphQL. GitHub data goes through `App\Github` with transients.
- Fetch only the fields you use. Fail soft when GitHub or DEV.to is down (cached or empty UI, not a white screen).
- Contact mail: `wp_mail` in `app/contact.php`. Cloud has no mail server; still keep the redirect and validation.

## Testing

- PHP: `vendor/bin/pint --test`. JS/CSS: `npm run build` after asset changes.
- Exercise the local site at `http://localhost:8080` (admin `admin` / `password`) when the change is visitor-facing.
- Do not delete existing posts or categories in seeds or tests.

## Comments and docs

- Comment non-obvious logic only. Use PHPDoc / JSDoc on public functions.
- Update `docs/FEATURES.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` when adding a user-visible feature.
- Sage docs first: https://roots.io/sage/docs/ and `docs/sage/`.
